## Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM) Images
The cross-sectional SEM image above shows clearly that there is no capping layer of perovskite formed by $\mathrm{CH_{3}N H_{3}S n I_{3}}$ in this device configuration. In a device with a $400\ \mathrm{nm}$ thick mesoporous $\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ , the perovskite material is contained solely within the pores of the $\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ . The delamination of the $\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ layer is as a result of fracturing the device. The formation of a capping layer in such a device is undesirable as a result of the short diffusion length of the material, which will cause recombination to occur on a faster timescale than charge extraction. Top view images of both $80\mathrm{nm}$ thick and $400\ \mathrm{nm}$ thick $\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ films infiltrated with $\mathrm{CH_{3}N H_{3}S n I_{3}}$ are shown below. This image very accurately illustrates the loss of the capping layer with increased film thickness.
